---
source: crates/gough-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: o.out
---
Read and write the local config file and contexts

Usage: gough config [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  get              Print the effective value of a config key
  set              Set a config key in the config file
  list             List effective config values and where each came from
  get-contexts     List named contexts
  current-context  Print the active context name
  use-context      Switch the active context
  set-context      Create or update a context
  delete-context   Delete a context
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -o, --output <FORMAT>  Output format: table, json, yaml or jsonpath=<RFC 9535 expression> [default: table]
  -q, --quiet            Suppress all output except errors
      --no-color         Disable colored output
      --cluster <URL>    Cluster API URL (env GOUGH_CLUSTER_URL); overrides the config file
      --context <NAME>   Named context from the config file (env GOUGH_CURRENT_CONTEXT)
  -v, --verbose          Log requests and diagnostics to stderr (tokens are masked)
      --ca-file <FILE>   Extra PEM CA bundle to trust for the cluster's TLS certificate
  -h, --help             Print help
